# Pluribus Design System

Swiss + Metro for layout and type; Material for spacing rhythm, elevation,
motion, and accessibility. When they conflict: typography and content structure
win over decoration; flat chrome over heavy shadows.

## Tokens

Define colors and scales only in `frontend/src/style.scss`. In atoms and
molecules, use `var(--*)` — no raw hex.

- Spacing: `var(--space-1)` … `var(--space-8)` (8dp grid)
- Type: `var(--text-xs)` … `var(--text-2xl)`, `var(--font-weight-*)`
- Radius: `var(--radius-sm|md|lg)` (Metro-leaning, subtle)
- Elevation: `var(--shadow-1)` or `var(--shadow-2)` only when needed
- Motion: `var(--motion-fast)`, `var(--motion-standard)`, `var(--ease-standard)`
- Semantic: `var(--color-primary)`, `var(--color-surface)`, `var(--color-outline)`, etc.

## Typography (Swiss + Metro)

- Headings carry page structure; avoid extra chrome to imply hierarchy.
- Use `Title` atom with `tag="h1"` … `h4` for the type scale.
- Body text: regular weight, comfortable line-height (`var(--line-height-normal)`).

## Layout and surfaces

- Align to 8dp spacing; prefer `gap` and padding from the scale.
- Nav and toolbars stay flat (Metro); segment with type and spacing before borders.
- Cards: `var(--color-surface)` + optional `var(--shadow-1)`; max 2 elevation levels.

## Interaction (Material)

- Transitions 120–200ms for hover/focus; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Always style `:focus-visible` with `var(--color-focus-ring)`.
- Buttons: primary / secondary / ghost / danger / link variants via `Button` atom.

## Atomic design

- `atoms/` → `molecules/` → `organisms/` → `views/` (pages).
- One-way imports only; no domain logic or data fetching in atoms.

## Examples

```vue
<!-- GOOD -->
<Button variant="primary">Save</Button>
```

```scss
/* BAD in atoms — hardcoded hex */
background: #2563eb;
```
